{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals","id":726593,"title":"Abyssals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-25T11:38:59-07:00","id":726593,"title":"Abyssals","content":"Mostly, just a place to discuss them.<br /> <br /> Personally, I find the old Mirror Charm concept to be super useful for Abyssals. It makes it very easy to stat up a fully fleshed Abyssal for play. Abyssalizing Solar charms is pretty easy, in most cases it is just a fluff change. I know Mirror has always been boring, and I can't wait until Abyssals gets publish and we get real Abyssal charms, but for now Mirror makes it really easy to throw down a serious Exalted threat, which is nice to have as a ST.<br /> <br /> I just wish we knew more about Necromancy so that I could throw around some serious Necromancers at my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:43:15-07:00","id":726626,"title":"","content":"I plan to just hack Necromancy into the Sorcery framework for now (since the First Arc villain my PC's are up against is an Abyssal Necromancer). Admittedly, I don't have the 2nd ed Abyssal book, so I'm not sure if going from the 1st ed book is going to make that easier or harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:45:11-07:00","id":726632,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, as a stopgap, Mirror is fine. When that's all you get, it sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:59:17-07:00","id":726665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=726626#post726626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I plan to just hack Necromancy into the Sorcery framework for now (since the First Arc villain my PC's are up against is an Abyssal Necromancer). Admittedly, I don't have the 2nd ed Abyssal book, so I'm not sure if going from the 1st ed book is going to make that easier or harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kind of getting the impression that Necromancy might just be a different kind of Sorcerous Initiation with its own Shaping Rituals, but the current spell list doesn't really fit Necromancy all that well, so I still need to make up Necromancy spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:12:44-07:00","id":726705,"title":"","content":"I like the Mirror tag in principle. Abyssals are supposed to be dark mirrors of Solars and that should be reflected in their charmset. In practice, I like charms that suggest the power and majesty of the Solars but are aesthetically and mechanically different enough that they don't quite work as Mirrors.<br /> <br /> Also, I have a player who I'm trying to introduce to Exalted. She likes the skulls and blood, sexy vampirey, champions of death stuff, but the more times she has to cross-reference another book, the more complaining I'm apt to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:21:19-07:00","id":726718,"title":"","content":"I kinda wonder if the Caste Ability spreads might end up being different between Solars and their Abyssal conterparts. Probably not a whole lot, and even then only in the three added Caste Abilities apart from the classic 2/2.5 spread. It could perhaps help the Abyssals move away from being &quot;we made these Solars listen to 'Bela Lugosi is Dead' fifty times and painted them with SPOOKYSAD&quot; and more their own thing (though still with definite ties to the Solars).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:38:51-07:00","id":726742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=726665#post726665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kind of getting the impression that Necromancy might just be a different kind of Sorcerous Initiation with its own Shaping Rituals, but the current spell list doesn't really fit Necromancy all that well, so I still need to make up Necromancy spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they did that, it wouldn't really be Necromancy any more. Necromancy was this dark mirror of Sorcery... not just another kind.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean that it won't happen - if the devs think turning it into just an initiation instead of having to write up new spells for it is a better use of writer's time and word count, I won't complain - Necromancy never seemed that impressive to me in previous editions, so there wouldn't be much to miss. On the other hand, I'd obviously prefer to see something that actually impresses me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:43:24-07:00","id":726757,"title":"","content":"I wish we knew more about this &quot;chivalry of death&quot; concept they speak of, personally. from the sound of it, it seems like Abyssals are less &quot;KILL THEM ALL&quot; and more spread despair around by withholding their blade at times.<br /> <br /> its a code of conduct right? if so, what are its tenets? Patience is obviously one of its virtues but the rest.....I hope the Abyssals book comes soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:51:54-07:00","id":726792,"title":"","content":"Word from the Devs is that Mirror is gone and Necromancy will be a whole other thing distinct from Sorcery. Details on that should be forthcoming in, what, 1-3 years, depending on whether the &quot;Year in Black&quot; comes right after Exigents and what delays happen.<br /> <br /> ... I don't plan to wait that long before using those concepts, and I don't have four developers and a few handfuls of playtesters to help me create hundreds of complexly interlocking pieces. So, just as the Corebook Nephrack just uses re-skinned Sorcery as stopgap &quot;Necromancy,&quot; so too will I use re-skinned Solar Charms as Abyssal stuff (and probably add a few custom high-Essence things) for the forseeable future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:54:18-07:00","id":726797,"title":"","content":"The &quot;chivalry of death&quot; thing is pretty interesting, yeah---it sounds a little like they're working in some classic villain tropes in a way, a little like how 2e Infernals had Urges that were basically cartoon villain habits (which I honestly thought was a cool idea).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:55:57-07:00","id":726800,"title":"","content":"In a funny way...the abyssal chivalry of death make them like Bugbears. In dnd, Bugbears are considered chaotic evil but it is their modus operandi, instead of killing an entire family, they will make sure that the person that would be hurt/despair the most stay alive. <br /> <br /> On top of it, from the description, they didn't say that the Abyssals were mirror of Solars...which might imply they might just be different exalts after all instead of being palette change to dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:59:26-07:00","id":726807,"title":"","content":"The sidebar on page 36 may be relevant... and a bit confusing. One thing I like especially: &quot;[...] a heightening of the real, such that colors burn brighter, scents are stronger, tastes are sweeter, <u>and all living things radiate with beauty and glory before the eyes of the reaper</u>.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's plenty of room for Abyssals declaring that only a true understanding of death can allow you to appreciate life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:09:19-07:00","id":726822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=726718#post726718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wonder if the Caste Ability spreads might end up being different between Solars and their Abyssal conterparts. Probably not a whole lot, and even then only in the three added Caste Abilities apart from the classic 2/2.5 spread. It could perhaps help the Abyssals move away from being &quot;we made these Solars listen to 'Bela Lugosi is Dead' fifty times and painted them with SPOOKYSAD&quot; and more their own thing (though still with definite ties to the Solars).</div> </div> </div> </div>What Abilities would you change between the Abyssal castes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:25:17-07:00","id":726863,"title":"","content":"That's a good question! Lemme help myself think this out.<br /> <br /> <b>DAWN</b>: Archery, Melee, Brawl*, Thrown, War, <i>Awareness</i>, <i>Dodge</i>, <i>Resistance</i><br /> <b>ZENITH</b>: Presence, Performance, Resistance, Integrity, Survival, <i>Athletics</i>, <i>Lore</i>, <i>War</i><br /> <b>TWILIGHT</b>: Medicine, Occult, Lore, Crafts, Investigation, <i>Bureaucracy</i>, <i>Linguistics</i>, <i>Integrity</i><br /> <b>NIGHT</b>: Stealth, Larceny, Awareness, Athletics, Dodge, <i>Investigation</i>, <i>Socialize</i>, <i>Ride</i><br /> <b>ECLIPSE</b>: Bureaucracy, Linguistics, Socialize, Sail, Ride, <i>Larceny</i>, <i>Occult</i>, <i>Presence</i><br /> <br /> Honestly, the problem with this good question is... I'm really not quite sure. Vague ideas flit through my head (letting Dusks have Athletics, giving War to someone other than Midnight) but this question isn't one I feel I have satisfactory answers to. I'm still very glad you asked it, though, because others might have good answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:33:12-07:00","id":726895,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't change anything for Abyssals, since they're the dark reflection of Solars, it would make sense for them to be basically identical at that stage of chargen.<br /> <br /> For Infernals, however, it very likely would be different. The trouble with this is that we don't know what the thesis for Infernals will be yet, or even the caste names, so everything related to this would be based off of a 2e paradigm that's not being retained. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:44:57-07:00","id":726915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=726895#post726895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't change anything for Abyssals, since they're the dark reflection of Solars, it would make sense for them to be basically identical at that stage of chargen.<br /> <br /> For Infernals, however, it very likely would be different. The trouble with this is that we don't know what the thesis for Infernals will be yet, or even the caste names, so everything related to this would be based off of a 2e paradigm that's not being retained.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope that the Infernal thesis is still freaky transhumanism, because that was fucking awesome, and if there's space for Alchemicals there sure as hell should be space for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:55:44-07:00","id":726957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=726895#post726895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't change anything for Abyssals, since they're the dark reflection of Solars, it would make sense for them to be basically identical at that stage of chargen.<br /> <br /> For Infernals, however, it very likely would be different. The trouble with this is that we don't know what the thesis for Infernals will be yet, or even the caste names, so everything related to this would be based off of a 2e paradigm that's not being retained.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Back in development, it was mentioned that Abyssals would have slightly different caste abilities from their Solar counterparts(And that all Solars had three powers, instead of Just Eclipse castes)<br /> <br /> As for Infernals, well, we know that the Yozi want them to be as Decadent as the Solars of the first age, we have a few comments that the Reclamation, if it exists, will be about the Infernals conquering Creation for themselves, there are some hints tht the Yozi would be living through the Green Sun Princes vicariously. Ability wise they have &quot;Like Solar Charms, but channeling the themes of the Yozi&quot; as well as some implications that they'll be emulating the Yozi, in general or individually. The Shinetais seem focused on some degree of shape-shifting, with both Yozi based forms and at least one custom form, as well as developing demonic mutations through at least one method. The Example infernal, the &quot;Dawn/Slayer&quot; equivalent, we have has &quot;Poisonous Green Fire&quot; powers, and her dragon-form/shintai has a Super Sonic scream, and her skin apparently has enough durability and enough resistance to extrme temperatures that she can walk around naked with no fear of harm whatsoever, so we've got at least three example &quot;fighty caste&quot; type powers.<br /> <br /> You could probably fake up so chargen level Princes with that info, though how accurate they'd be is a matter of debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 10-25-2015, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:58:07-07:00","id":726962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=726915#post726915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope that the Infernal thesis is still freaky transhumanism, because that was fucking awesome, and if there's space for Alchemicals there sure as hell should be space for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a lesser extent than before, but all of the &quot;limited&quot; previews are pointing to yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T14:00:27-07:00","id":726964,"title":"","content":"Yeah but considering 2e Infernals used Yozi Charms and were members of Castes explicitly tainted and influenced by the Yozis, it's really hard to say what direction they'll take this edition. Even if their themes might still involve transhumanism, they'll be in quite a different shape just with the two things I previously mentioned changing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T14:10:53-07:00","id":727035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=726964#post726964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but considering 2e Infernals used Yozi Charms and were members of Castes explicitly tainted and influenced by the Yozis, it's really hard to say what direction they'll take this edition. Even if their themes might still involve transhumanism, they'll be in quite a different shape just with the two things I previously mentioned changing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's been confirmed that Green Sun Princes are still corrupted Solars, and are still corrupted solars because the stuff created by UCS is still hella fucking awesome, and Yozi still have limited creativity and ability create Exalts of their own.<br /> <br /> So, I'd imagine that the basic chassis will still be at least superficially similar to the basic chassis of the Solars.<br /> <br /> Although maybe we should move this conversation to the &quot;Infernals&quot; thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T18:10:10-07:00","id":727630,"title":"","content":"I kinda have a question about Abyssals, but it's possible the Devs are the only ones who can answer this. I dunno.<br /> <br /> Is it still true that Abyssals are the stolen, corrupted Exaltations of Solars? I got a chance to go through the PDF a couple days ago, but I couldn't find that bit. I'm planning a game for when I can actually buy the dang thing, and knowing one way or the other kinda has a serious effect on certain NPCs I'll be creating for the game. Is that in the book? If not, urg, Deeeeevs? Clarification?<br /> <br /> (Knowing whether Lunar Bond is still a thing would be super helpful too, though not the point of this thread in particular...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T18:17:04-07:00","id":727661,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, back in the Abyssals thread...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=726957#post726957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in development, it was mentioned that Abyssals would have slightly different caste abilities from their Solar counterparts</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not heard this or I'd forgotten. What would be the point of rearranging caste abilities?<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I'm planning on Mirroring up the Abyssal Charms. With as many Charms that the new Core has provided, it shouldn't be too difficult for me to come up with Abyssals who have Solar Charms different from the PCs fluffed up with the death/darkness vibe to make them seem really different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T18:43:37-07:00","id":727742,"title":"","content":"In my opinion if the death knight /abyssals are still about death and Necromancy...maybe having all castes spread horrors/despairs: Performance might be a common ability to represent how they can spread their terror across the land in spectacular ways.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T18:43:43-07:00","id":727743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=727630#post727630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda have a question about Abyssals, but it's possible the Devs are the only ones who can answer this. I dunno.<br /> <br /> Is it still true that Abyssals are the stolen, corrupted Exaltations of Solars? I got a chance to go through the PDF a couple days ago, but I couldn't find that bit. I'm planning a game for when I can actually buy the dang thing, and knowing one way or the other kinda has a serious effect on certain NPCs I'll be creating for the game. Is that in the book? If not, urg, Deeeeevs? Clarification?<br /> <br /> (Knowing whether Lunar Bond is still a thing would be super helpful too, though not the point of this thread in particular...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Since they still have the Solar Castes (altered appropriately) they probably still are the stolen, corrupted Solar Exaltations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T19:25:24-07:00","id":727885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=727661#post727661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, back in the Abyssals thread...<br /> <br /> <br /> I had not heard this or I'd forgotten. What would be the point of rearranging caste abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be because I accidentally used the wrong term.<br /> <br /> I meant Anima abilities. The Abyssal castes would have slightly different anima abilities from their Solar counter parts, as has been confirmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T01:14:58-07:00","id":728104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=726895#post726895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't change anything for Abyssals, since they're the dark reflection of Solars, it would make sense for them to be basically identical at that stage of chargen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling you say that because you haven't known the annoyance of having to constantly read someone else's book to know or recall what your own charms do. Never fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T01:27:34-07:00","id":728120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=728104#post728104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling you say that because you haven't known the annoyance of having to constantly read someone else's book to know or recall what your own charms do. Never fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>&gt;Not building a character that requires referencing eight rulebooks, a dozen periodicals and twenty pages of houserules.<br /> <br /> *sigh* I don't even know what this hobby <i>is</i> anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As you are now, so once was I,<br /> As I am now, so you will be.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/285-andonno","name":"Andonno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T04:30:25-07:00","id":728357,"title":"","content":"A while ago, one of the writers (I think it was Hatewheel) said that Abyssals would start out with very similar charms to Solars, to cover basic competences, but they'd build towards very different, more evocative pinnacle charms.<br /> Considering how awkward it could be to ensure your Infernal covered basic competences, this seems a good idea to me. It seems appropriately thematic too.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T06:29:25-07:00","id":728655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=728104#post728104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling you say that because you haven't known the annoyance of having to constantly read someone else's book to know or recall what your own charms do. Never fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it doesn't have to be that way. They could do a return to 1e, where Abyssal charms early in the trees were obvious Solar mirrors, but were different enough you couldn't just write &quot;look at the Core.&quot; And they built to different ends; by the pinnacle Charms they were... very different.<br /> <br /> One of the things I loved about 1e Abyssals was their various poor-mans-perfect effects; because they didn't usually make themselves better but their enemies worse; if you were willing to burn the essence to reduce dice pools all the way to zero, you could do crazy shit like just stand there smirking as your death essence enveloped your foes and caused their blows to go awry. Then you'd murder them right in the face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T06:43:08-07:00","id":728670,"title":"","content":"Mirror was great in theory. In practice, this just meant that instead of getting new Abyssal charms, authors would just write new Solar charms and slap the Mirror keyword on it.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of the Mirror keyword encourages authors to make unique Abyssal charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T07:36:26-07:00","id":728821,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of starting similarly and then having really different, cool stuff that the Solars <i>don't get</i> (cough cough the backwards-Mirroring that kept giving Solars unspoopified Abyssal stuff in 2e). That'd help push the &quot;dark reflections of Solars but still with their own identity beyond being like sunbros but frowny&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T07:47:05-07:00","id":728870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=728655#post728655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it doesn't have to be that way. They could do a return to 1e, where Abyssal charms early in the trees were obvious Solar mirrors, but were different enough you couldn't just write &quot;look at the Core.&quot; And they built to different ends; by the pinnacle Charms they were... very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look at the Abyssal charms in the back of the book, some of the most basic ones are identical to Solar charms (but don't say &quot;just look at Solar charm X&quot;), some are similar but slightly different, and some are completely different. That sounds similar to what you're describing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T09:09:54-07:00","id":729093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/726593-abyssals?p=728870#post728870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you look at the Abyssal charms in the back of the book, some of the most basic ones are identical to Solar charms (but don't say &quot;just look at Solar charm X&quot;), some are similar but slightly different, and some are completely different. That sounds similar to what you're describing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, and it makes me happy in my various places.<br /> <br /> It's hard to have what I feel are well-developed opinions on this. I mean... that doesn't stop me. But the Charm design space has been jacked for so long. They made greater or lesser errors in every single major fatsplat of 2e except for Infernals, which were a triumphant miracle of interesting design... that were immediately crippled by 2.5 because they had to be.<br /> <br /> On the other hand that new Solar design space at least indicates things are going to be well thought out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}